        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The chain rule can be used to differentiate exponential functions like \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: y = e^{3x}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The chain rule can be used to differentiate exponential functions like\n[MATH: y = e^{3x}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: y = e^u, \\qquad u = 3x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n[MATH: y = e^u, \\qquad u = 3x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:</p>",
            "readable_text": "We can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (dy)/(dx)|= (dy)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = (d)/(du)(e^{u}) \u22c5 (d)/(dx)(3x); = e^{u} \u22c5 3; = 3e^{u}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: (dy)/(dx)|= (dy)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = (d)/(du)(e^{u}) \u22c5 (d)/(dx)(3x); = e^{u} \u22c5 3; = 3e^{u}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Substituting <span class=\"math\">[MATH: u=3x,]</span> we obtain the final result:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Substituting [MATH: u=3x,] we obtain the final result:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (dy)/(dx)|= 3e^{3x}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: (dy)/(dx)|= 3e^{3x}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nThe chain rule can be used to differentiate exponential functions like\n[MATH: y = e^{3x}.]\n\nContent:\nFirst, notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n[MATH: y = e^u, \\qquad u = 3x.]\n\nContent:\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (dy)/(dx)|= (dy)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = (d)/(du)(e^{u}) \u22c5 (d)/(dx)(3x); = e^{u} \u22c5 3; = 3e^{u}]\n\nContent:\nSubstituting [MATH: u=3x,] we obtain the final result:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (dy)/(dx)|= 3e^{3x}]"
      },
