        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Calculate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f&#x27;(x)]</span> if <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(x) = e^{5x +4}.]</span> </p>",
            "readable_text": "Calculate [MATH: f'(x)] if [MATH: f(x) = e^{5x +4}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we express <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(x)]</span> as the composite function\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: f = e^u, \\qquad u=5x+4.]</span></p><p>Differentiating gives</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = e^u,\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} =5.]</span></p><p>We now apply the chain rule, and get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (df)/(dx)|= (df)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = e^{u} \u22c5 5; = 5e^{u}; = 5e^{5x + 4}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we express [MATH: f(x)] as the composite function\n[MATH: f = e^u, \\qquad u=5x+4.]\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = e^u,\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} =5.]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n[MATH: (df)/(dx)|= (df)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = e^{u} \u22c5 5; = 5e^{u}; = 5e^{5x + 4}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: f'(x)] if [MATH: f(x) = e^{5x +4}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we express [MATH: f(x)] as the composite function\n[MATH: f = e^u, \\qquad u=5x+4.]\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = e^u,\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} =5.]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n[MATH: (df)/(dx)|= (df)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = e^{u} \u22c5 5; = 5e^{u}; = 5e^{5x + 4}.]"
      },
