          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we express <span class=\"math\">[MATH: y]</span> as the composite function</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: y = 3\\cdot 2^u, \\qquad u=1-x.]</span></p><p>Differentiating gives</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = 3\\cdot 2^u\\ln(2),\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} =-1.]</span></p><p>We now apply the chain rule, and get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (dy)/(dx)|= (dy)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = 3 \u22c5 2^{u}\\ln (2) \u22c5 (\u2212 1); = \u2212 3 \u22c5 2^{u}\\ln (2); = \u2212 3 \u22c5 2^{1 \u2212 x}\\ln (2).]</span></p>",
