        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nGiven that [MATH: y= 3\\cdot 2^{1 - x},] find [MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we express [MATH: y] as the composite function\n\n[MATH: y = 3\\cdot 2^u, \\qquad u=1-x.]\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = 3\\cdot 2^u\\ln(2),\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} =-1.]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n[MATH: (dy)/(dx)|= (dy)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = 3 \u22c5 2^{u}\\ln (2) \u22c5 (\u2212 1); = \u2212 3 \u22c5 2^{u}\\ln (2); = \u2212 3 \u22c5 2^{1 \u2212 x}\\ln (2).]"
